# WINDSURF AGENTIC RULES — TECHMINDDEV
# Universal rules for Cascade / Windsurf Agent

## 1. ARCHITECTURE & CODE QUALITY
- Follow Clean Architecture and Feature-First folder organization.
- Keep all files under 200 lines of code. Split into sub-components when exceeding this limit.
- Never write business or database logic directly inside UI widgets or view components.
- Use strict typing (TypeScript / Dart) and validate all inputs with Zod / Pydantic.

## 2. DATABASE & PERSISTENCE
- Primary keys must use UUIDv7 (`uuid_generate_v7()`) or ULID. Never use exposed sequential integers.
- All Supabase/PostgreSQL tables MUST enable Row Level Security (RLS).
- Avoid N+1 queries by using explicit JOINs or `whereIn`.

## 3. EXTERNAL APIS & RATE LIMITS (ANTI-BAN RULES)
- Never make direct external API calls (YouTube, Google Maps, OpenAI) on frontend render without Cache-First layer.
- Always apply batching (up to 50 IDs per request) and throttling (max 2 req/s via p-limit).
- Include Exponential Backoff with Jitter for HTTP 429 and 403 (QuotaExceeded) errors.

## 4. SECURITY
- NEVER hardcode API keys or secrets in frontend code. Always use backend `.env` variables.
- Validate all incoming webhooks using cryptographic signature verification (HMAC).
